      <!-- SECTION 01 EN -->
      <h2 id="sec-what-is-en">01 · WHAT IS AUTOMATION STUDIO?</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Automation Studio</strong> is a Salesforce Marketing Cloud Engagement application that enables you to automate marketing and data management processes using Activities organized within Automations.
      </p>
      <p>
        Through this tool, you can transfer and prepare files, transform data using queries, manage data tables, and coordinate bulk sends or scheduled interactions. It is not limited to running SQL queries; it encompasses a broad set of tasks for moving, transforming, and administering data.
      </p>

      <div class="callout tip">
        <div class="callout-label">🏭 THE AUTOMATED FACTORY ANALOGY</div>
        To visualize how it operates, think of Automation Studio as <strong>an assembly line in an automated factory</strong>:
        <br/><br/>
        • The <strong>raw materials</strong> entering the line are incoming data records or files.<br/>
        • Each <strong>workstation</strong> performs a specific task (clean, filter, package) → <strong>Activity</strong>.<br/>
        • The workstations are arranged in <strong>sequential stages</strong> along the conveyor belt → <strong>Steps</strong>.<br/>
        • The <strong>entire assembly line</strong> running from start to finish is your <strong>Automation</strong>.
      </div>

      <div class="callout tip" style="margin-top:1.2rem;">
        <div class="callout-label">💡 IN A NUTSHELL</div>
        Automation Studio enables you to chain and automate Marketing Cloud Engagement tasks within planned, structured workflows.
      </div>

      <!-- SECTION 02 EN -->
      <h2 id="sec-what-for-en">02 · WHAT IS IT USED FOR IN BUSINESS?</h2>
      <p>
        In everyday enterprise operations, marketing teams must process, clean, and update large volumes of data before launching campaigns. Automation Studio handles the background technical tasks that keep the platform synchronized and data ready for activation.
      </p>
      <p>
        Common enterprise use cases include:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Importing or copying data</strong>: Ingesting daily customer or order files from secure storage, or copying records across Data Extensions.</li>
        <li><strong>Preparing and segmenting audiences</strong>: Identifying high-value VIP customers, abandoned carts from 48 hours ago, or subscribers needing re-engagement.</li>
        <li><strong>Transferring and protecting files</strong>: Moving files to and from the SFMC Safehouse, unzipping compressed files, or applying PGP decryption.</li>
        <li><strong>Running custom logic</strong>: Executing Server-Side JavaScript (SSJS) in Script Activities to orchestrate API calls or validate business rules.</li>
        <li><strong>Feeding Journey Builder</strong>: Preparing and refreshing the Data Extensions used to admit contacts into multichannel journeys.</li>
        <li><strong>Extracting data</strong>: Exporting consolidated tables or tracking data (opens, clicks, bounces) for external analytics and audits.</li>
      </ul>

      <div style="background:var(--bg-elevated);border-left:4px solid var(--neon-cyan);padding:1rem 1.2rem;border-radius:0 var(--radius) var(--radius) 0;margin:1.2rem 0;">
        <span style="color:var(--neon-cyan);font-weight:bold;display:block;margin-bottom:0.3rem;">🏢 Real Business Scenario:</span>
        <span style="color:var(--text-secondary);font-size:0.9rem;">
          Every night at 02:00 AM, a company receives a file with the previous day's new customer signups. Automation Studio detects it, imports it into a Data Extension, runs a query to classify customers by tier, and prepares the final audience for the morning welcome campaign.
        </span>
      </div>

      <div class="callout tip" style="margin-top:1.2rem;">
        <div class="callout-label">💡 IN A NUTSHELL</div>
        Automation Studio autonomously executes technical backend processes and data movements to support marketing strategies.
      </div>

