      <!-- SECTION 12 EN -->
      <h2 id="sec-best-practices-en">12 · INITIAL BEST PRACTICES</h2>
      <p>
        When architecting your first automations, distinguish between platform requirements and recommended best practices:
      </p>

      <div style="background:var(--bg-elevated);border:1px solid var(--border-dim);border-radius:var(--radius);padding:1.2rem;margin:1.5rem 0;">
        <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:1rem;">
          <div>
            <span style="color:var(--neon-pink);font-weight:bold;font-size:0.9rem;">🔒 PLATFORM REQUIREMENTS</span>
            <ul style="font-size:0.85rem;color:var(--text-secondary);margin:0.4rem 0 0 0;padding-left:1.2rem;">
              <li>Every SQL Query Activity requires an existing target Data Extension with a designated data action (Append, Update, or Overwrite).</li>
              <li>You can include multiple Verification Activities in the same Step, but a Verification Activity cannot share that Step with other activity types.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--border-dim);padding-top:0.8rem;">
            <span style="color:var(--neon-green);font-weight:bold;font-size:0.9rem;">✨ RECOMMENDED BEST PRACTICES</span>
            <ul style="font-size:0.85rem;color:var(--text-secondary);margin:0.4rem 0 0 0;padding-left:1.2rem;">
              <li><strong>Clear naming conventions</strong>: Use descriptive names and clear prefixes for Automations and Activities (e.g. <code>SYNC_Customers_Daily_02AM</code>).</li>
              <li><strong>Separate dependent activities</strong>: Do not place an activity in the same Step as an activity that produces its required data.</li>
              <li><strong>Test before scheduling</strong>: Use the manual execution option (Run Once) to verify activities succeed before enabling a production Schedule.</li>
              <li><strong>Caution with active automations</strong>: Exercise caution when making changes to active Automations, and review their status and history after updating configurations.</li>
              <li><strong>Review execution logs</strong>: Check the run history (Activity Log / History) after initial runs to verify row counts and timing.</li>
              <li><strong>Modularity</strong>: Avoid creating excessively large Automations if the pipeline can be divided into clean, independent flows.</li>
              <li><strong>Document purpose</strong>: Include concise descriptions explaining what each automation accomplishes to simplify team maintenance.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="callout tip" style="margin-top:1.2rem;">
        <div class="callout-label">💡 IN A NUTSHELL</div>
        Step sequencing, clear naming, and pre-testing with Run Once form the bedrock of reliable automation architecture.
      </div>

      <!-- SECTION 13 EN -->
      <h2 id="sec-use-cases-en">13 · REAL-WORLD USE CASES</h2>

      <div class="usecase-box">
        <div class="usecase-box-header">
          <span>✔️</span>
          <span>USE CASE: Nightly Synchronization with Encrypted File</span>
        </div>
        <p style="font-size:0.88rem;color:var(--text-secondary);margin:0">
          <strong>Problem:</strong> A business exports a PGP-encrypted customer file (<code>new_customers.csv.pgp</code>) to secure external storage and needs records decrypted and loaded into Marketing Cloud before 08:00 AM.<br/>
          <strong>Automation Studio Solution:</strong> A 03:00 AM Schedule triggers a 3-step pipeline: (1) <em>File Transfer Activity</em> decrypts the encrypted file into the Safehouse; (2) <em>Data Copy or Import</em> loads the decrypted records into <code>Staging_Customers</code>; (3) <em>SQL Query</em> updates the master Data Extension.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="usecase-box">
        <div class="usecase-box-header">
          <span>✔️</span>
          <span>USE CASE: Periodic Identification of Inactive Contacts</span>
        </div>
        <p style="font-size:0.88rem;color:var(--text-secondary);margin:0">
          <strong>Problem:</strong> Repeatedly emailing unengaged contacts can negatively affect overall engagement and deliverability strategies.<br/>
          <strong>Automation Studio Solution:</strong> A weekly Sunday automation executes an <em>SQL Query</em> reading system Data Views (such as <code>_Open</code> or <code>_Sent</code>), identifies contacts without recent interaction, and populates an exclusion Data Extension to adjust upcoming campaign sends.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- SECTION 14 EN -->
      <h2 id="sec-quiz-en">14 · CHECK YOUR KNOWLEDGE</h2>
      <p>
        Check your comprehension by answering these 4 key questions (click each card to reveal the explanation):
      </p>

      <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.8rem;margin:1.5rem 0;">

        <details style="background:var(--bg-elevated);border:1px solid var(--border-dim);border-radius:var(--radius);padding:1rem;">
          <summary style="cursor:pointer;color:var(--neon-yellow);font-weight:bold;font-size:0.92rem;">
            1. What is the difference between an Automation and an Activity?
          </summary>
          <div style="margin-top:0.8rem;font-size:0.88rem;color:var(--text-secondary);line-height:1.5;border-top:1px solid var(--border-dim);padding-top:0.8rem;">
            An <strong>Automation</strong> is the complete workflow defining how and when a process runs. An <strong>Activity</strong> is a discrete, reusable technical task (like an SQL Query or data import) executed within a Step of that Automation.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details style="background:var(--bg-elevated);border:1px solid var(--border-dim);border-radius:var(--radius);padding:1rem;">
          <summary style="cursor:pointer;color:var(--neon-yellow);font-weight:bold;font-size:0.92rem;">
            2. What role does a Step play within an Automation?
          </summary>
          <div style="margin-top:0.8rem;font-size:0.88rem;color:var(--text-secondary);line-height:1.5;border-top:1px solid var(--border-dim);padding-top:0.8rem;">
            A <strong>Step</strong> is a stage within the Automation that groups one or more Activities. Steps execute sequentially one after another, structuring dependency order across tasks.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details style="background:var(--bg-elevated);border:1px solid var(--border-dim);border-radius:var(--radius);padding:1rem;">
          <summary style="cursor:pointer;color:var(--neon-yellow);font-weight:bold;font-size:0.92rem;">
            3. If an SQL Query generates a Data Extension that another Activity requires, should they be in the same Step or consecutive Steps?
          </summary>
          <div style="margin-top:0.8rem;font-size:0.88rem;color:var(--text-secondary);line-height:1.5;border-top:1px solid var(--border-dim);padding-top:0.8rem;">
            <strong>In consecutive Steps.</strong> Activities in the same Step can execute simultaneously. If one activity requires the output of another, they must be separated into different Steps to ensure precedence.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details style="background:var(--bg-elevated);border:1px solid var(--border-dim);border-radius:var(--radius);padding:1rem;">
          <summary style="cursor:pointer;color:var(--neon-yellow);font-weight:bold;font-size:0.92rem;">
            4. What is the conceptual difference between File Transfer and Data Copy or Import?
          </summary>
          <div style="margin-top:0.8rem;font-size:0.88rem;color:var(--text-secondary);line-height:1.5;border-top:1px solid var(--border-dim);padding-top:0.8rem;">
            <strong>File Transfer</strong> prepares or moves the physical file (moving across storage locations, unzipping, encrypting, or decrypting). <strong>Data Copy or Import</strong> works with the data inside the file to insert or copy records into Marketing Cloud tables (a standard CSV does not strictly require File Transfer prior to ingestion).
          </div>
        </details>

      </div>

      <!-- SECTION 15 EN -->
      <h2 id="sec-challenge-en">15 · ARCADE CHALLENGE</h2>

      <div class="challenge-box">
        <div class="challenge-box-header">
          <span class="challenge-box-icon">🎮 </span>
          <div>
            <div class="challenge-box-title">MISSION: Build Your First Conceptual Automation</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p style="font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--text-secondary);margin-bottom:1rem;">
          <strong>The Scenario:</strong> Every morning, an external system uploads a compressed file <code>customers.zip</code> to your Enhanced FTP. The archive contains <code>customers.csv</code>. The automation must detect its arrival, unzip it, load the records into <code>Staging_Customers</code>, and generate the <code>Audience_Final</code> Data Extension ready for the daily campaign.
          <br/><br/>
          <strong>Your Challenge:</strong> Place the following 5 building blocks in their logical sequence across Starting Source, Steps, and Outcome:
        </p>

        <div style="background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border:1px dashed var(--border-dim);padding:0.8rem;border-radius:var(--radius);font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:0.82rem;color:var(--neon-yellow);margin-bottom:1.2rem;">
          [A] Data Copy or Import (Loads customers.csv into Staging_Customers)<br/>
          [B] File Transfer Activity (Unzips customers.zip)<br/>
          [C] Starting Source: File Drop (Detects arrival of customers.zip on Enhanced FTP)<br/>
          [D] Data Extension Audience_Final (Final outcome)<br/>
          [E] SQL Query Activity (Cross-references Staging_Customers data and generates Audience_Final)
        </div>

        <details style="font-size:0.85rem;">
          <summary style="cursor:pointer;color:var(--neon-yellow);margin-bottom:0.75rem;font-weight:bold;"> View solution and explanation</summary>
          
          <!-- DIAGRAM D EN: VISUAL CHALLENGE SOLUTION (HTML/CSS) -->
          <div style="background:var(--bg-elevated);border:1px solid var(--border-dim);border-radius:var(--radius);padding:1.2rem;margin-top:0.8rem;">
            <div style="max-width:520px;margin:0 auto;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.35rem;">
              
              <!-- Starting Source -->
              <div style="background:rgba(255,140,0,0.1);border:1.5px solid var(--neon-orange);border-radius:6px;padding:0.6rem 0.8rem;text-align:center;">
                <span style="font-size:0.72rem;color:var(--neon-orange);font-weight:bold;display:block;">STARTING SOURCE</span>
                <span style="font-size:0.85rem;color:var(--text-primary);font-weight:bold;">[C] Starting Source: File Drop (detects 'customers.zip' on Enhanced FTP)</span>
              </div>

              <div style="display:flex;justify-content:center;color:var(--neon-yellow);"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><line x1="12" y1="2" x2="12" y2="18"></line><polyline points="18 12 12 18 6 12"></polyline></svg></div>

              <!-- Step 1 -->
              <div style="background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid var(--border-dim);border-radius:6px;padding:0.6rem 0.8rem;text-align:center;">
                <span style="font-size:0.72rem;color:var(--neon-yellow);font-weight:bold;display:block;">STEP 1 · ACTIVITY</span>
                <span style="font-size:0.85rem;color:var(--text-primary);">[B] File Transfer Activity: Manage File → Unzip (unzips 'customers.zip')</span>
              </div>

              <div style="display:flex;justify-content:center;color:var(--neon-yellow);"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><line x1="12" y1="2" x2="12" y2="18"></line><polyline points="18 12 12 18 6 12"></polyline></svg></div>

              <!-- Step 2 -->
              <div style="background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid var(--border-dim);border-radius:6px;padding:0.6rem 0.8rem;text-align:center;">
                <span style="font-size:0.72rem;color:var(--neon-yellow);font-weight:bold;display:block;">STEP 2 · ACTIVITY</span>
                <span style="font-size:0.85rem;color:var(--text-primary);">[A] Data Copy or Import: loads 'customers.csv' into 'Staging_Customers'</span>
              </div>

              <div style="display:flex;justify-content:center;color:var(--neon-yellow);"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><line x1="12" y1="2" x2="12" y2="18"></line><polyline points="18 12 12 18 6 12"></polyline></svg></div>

              <!-- Step 3 -->
              <div style="background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid var(--border-dim);border-radius:6px;padding:0.6rem 0.8rem;text-align:center;">
                <span style="font-size:0.72rem;color:var(--neon-yellow);font-weight:bold;display:block;">STEP 3 · ACTIVITY</span>
                <span style="font-size:0.85rem;color:var(--text-primary);">[E] SQL Query Activity: joins 'Staging_Customers' and generates 'Audience_Final'</span>
              </div>

              <div style="display:flex;justify-content:center;color:var(--neon-green);"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><line x1="12" y1="2" x2="12" y2="18"></line><polyline points="18 12 12 18 6 12"></polyline></svg></div>

              <!-- Final outcome -->
              <div style="background:rgba(0,255,136,0.08);border:1.5px solid var(--neon-green);border-radius:6px;padding:0.6rem 0.8rem;text-align:center;">
                <span style="font-size:0.72rem;color:var(--neon-green);font-weight:bold;display:block;">FINAL OUTCOME</span>
                <span style="font-size:0.85rem;color:var(--text-primary);font-weight:bold;">[D] Data Extension 'Audience_Final' ready</span>
              </div>

            </div>
            
            <p style="font-size:0.82rem;color:var(--text-secondary);margin-top:1rem;line-height:1.5;">
              <strong>Sequence rationale (C → B → A → E → D):</strong> File Drop [C] is the Starting Source triggering execution upon detecting <code>customers.zip</code>; it is not an Activity, so it does not occupy a Step. In the <strong>Step 1</strong>, <em>File Transfer Activity</em> [B] is essential to unzip the compressed file and extract <code>customers.csv</code>. In <strong>Step 2</strong>, <em>Data Copy or Import</em> [A] reads the extracted CSV and populates <code>Staging_Customers</code>. In <strong>Step 3</strong>, <em>SQL Query Activity</em> [E] processes and segments staging records to generate the final audience. Finally, Data Extension <code>Audience_Final</code> [D] is the resulting target table ready for the campaign.
            </p>
